    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0302" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4873: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-08T11:00:00+01:00">August 8, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 8—8:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>101. Yesterday afternoon a Council of Ministers was held with the King presiding.
                    The question at issue was the adherence of Belgium <pb facs="0303" n="189"
                        xml:id="pg189"/> to the final protocol drawn up in London by the Committee
                    of Experts.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d135-f1"/> The Belgian Foreign Office informs
                    me today in strictest confidence that the outcome of the meeting was completely
                    satisfactory. The Foreign Office wants no publicity on the German attitude at
                    London before the official statement which will be made after the final meeting
                    there. This telegram has been repeated to Livesey.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
